  "name": "Check cold email compliance with Precleared before drafting in Gmail",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "5b7016c6-5e21-57ea-8bd0-8b49aa7c7b42",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -980,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Check cold email compliance before drafting in Gmail\n\nChecks every lead with [Precleared](https://precleared.dev) before an email is written, so you only draft emails the law allows: UK PECR and GDPR, US CAN-SPAM, Canada's CASL, Germany's UWG and French rules.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Sample leads** gives three test leads. Swap in Google Sheets, Airtable or your CRM.\n2. **Check with Precleared** asks whether a cold email to each address is allowed. It returns a verdict, the rule with its source, what the footer must include and a signed receipt id.\n3. If the verdict is `ok_to_email`, **Write the email** adds your footer (company, postal address, opt-out line) and keeps Precleared's requirement as `footer_rule`. **Create Gmail draft** saves it for you to review.\n4. Anything else goes to **Hold back**, with the reason and the next step.\n\n### Setup\n1. Fill in **Your settings**: your country (GB or US), name, company, postal address, opt-out line and what you offer.\n2. Connect Gmail in **Create Gmail draft**.\n3. Run it. The sample domains have no mail server, so they land in **Hold back**. Then point **Map lead fields** at your own leads.\n\nNo account needed: 10 free checks a day. A free key from [precleared.dev/get-key](https://precleared.dev/get-key) gives 25 a day, and packs add more. To use a key, set **Check with Precleared** to Header Auth with the name `Authorization` and the value `Bearer pc_live_...`.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Change the wording in **Write the email**, and check your footer meets `footer_rule`.\n- Switch the draft to a send once you trust it.\n- Save the receipt id with each lead as proof of the check.\n\nPrecleared is decision support with sources, not legal advice."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
